      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start. I really want to focus on the idea that any state intervention—even for \"safety\" or \"misinformation\"—is fundamentally a move to control which ideas are allowed to exist. Are there specific philosophers or legal theorists who argue that the state itself is too inherently biased to ever be a neutral arbiter of digital speech?",
