      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. so basically, if we accept that the state is inherently biased, then any attempt at \"regulating\" the internet for the sake of truth or safety is just a way for the people in power to silence their opponents. how would you summarize the core moral failure of the \"safety and misinformation\" defense from that perspective?",
